# Blood and Glory (windurst 87): the qm3 and Cailleach Bheur in Ifrit's Cauldron with GM-set states. Available with the
# map (GM): no handler, nothing pops (the qm3's default NOTHING_OUT_OF_ORDINARY). Accepted without the map: nil. The
# map: Cailleach Bheur pops; the map taken by GM before the kill: her death sets nothing, so the next qm3 talk (no map,
# killed_wsnm 0) is nil. The map again, and a wait for her body to go (popFromQM needs her despawned): she pops again;
# the quest deleted by GM (available) before the kill: no death handler, killed_wsnm not set; accepted again by GM,
# after the wait the qm3 (the map, killed_wsnm 0): she pops a third time, no Annals of Truth.
lists IfritsCauldron/qm3/onTrigger
char zone=IfritsCauldron pos=118.8,20.0,141.8 job=WAR lvl=75
login
keyitem MapToTheAnnalsOfTruth
trigger qm3                                         # available, the map: no handler; nothing pops; NOTHING_OUT_OF_ORDINARY
quest Windurst.BloodAndGlory accepted
delkeyitem MapToTheAnnalsOfTruth
trigger qm3                                         # accepted, no map: nil; NOTHING_OUT_OF_ORDINARY
keyitem MapToTheAnnalsOfTruth
trigger qm3                                         # the map: Cailleach Bheur pops (claimed); SENSE_OMINOUS_PRESENCE
delkeyitem MapToTheAnnalsOfTruth
kill CAILLEACH_BHEUR                                # no map: killed_wsnm not set
trigger qm3                                         # no map, killed_wsnm 0: nil; NOTHING_OUT_OF_ORDINARY
keyitem MapToTheAnnalsOfTruth
tick 15000                                          # her body despawns: one zone tick per tick statement
tick 15000
tick 15000
trigger qm3                                         # the map: she pops again; SENSE_OMINOUS_PRESENCE
quest Windurst.BloodAndGlory available
kill CAILLEACH_BHEUR                                # the quest available: no death handler; killed_wsnm not set
quest Windurst.BloodAndGlory accepted
tick 15000
tick 15000
tick 15000
trigger qm3                                         # killed_wsnm 0, the map: she pops again; SENSE_OMINOUS_PRESENCE
